explicitly credits humour's failure as inversion rather than excess and instructs markers not
to penalise it, which matches topic-02.mdx. No conflicting key or criterion found.

ERQ rubrics (unit-assessment.mdx 245+): marked out of 20 across four criteria with
Limited/Adequate/Strong bands that differ in substance rather than in adverbs, and an overall
cap of 10 unless the analysis or evaluation criterion reaches Adequate. That is a real
higher-order gate, not a label.

